# Generated blueprint candidates, at the subject root and inside each view folder.
# The art director reviews them and keeps only the chosen image as reference.<ext>.
blueprints/*/*/*.png
blueprints/*/*/*.webp
blueprints/*/*/*.jpg
blueprints/*/*/*.jpeg
blueprints/*/*/*/*

# The chosen identity image, the raw source, and the subject log are committed.
!blueprints/*/*/reference.webp
!blueprints/*/*/notes.md
!blueprints/*/*/manifest.json

# The crop and the annotated copies are derived: they rebuild from the reference at any time.
# The files that record the decision -- dimensions.json and measurements.json -- are committed.
!blueprints/*/*/dimensions.json
!blueprints/*/*/measurements.json

# The crop is NOT derived scratch: it is the modeling input. The viewer's calque and the hull tracer
# both read `cropped/<view>.webp`, and both convert its pixels to millimetres, so losing it means
# re-arbitrating every scale. It is written lossless and verified by crop_reference.py.
!blueprints/*/*/*/cropped/
!blueprints/*/*/*/cropped/*.webp
!blueprints/*/*/*/cropped/manifest.json

# Selected views are also committed.
!blueprints/*/*/*/reference.png
!blueprints/*/*/*/reference.webp
!blueprints/*/*/*/reference.jpg
!blueprints/*/*/*/reference.jpeg

# A finalized reference is WebP. The original format is converted, verified, then removed: the
# `.jpg`, `.jpeg` and `.png` whitelist lines above stay only for subjects that were locked before
# the format rule, and for a candidate that is promoted before its conversion.

# Every candidate of a subject is committed: the art director reviews the results on a machine with a
# display, and the folder is the record of the workflow's progress. A draft stays local, because
# `blueprints/drafts/` is ignored; the T0016 draft candidate is kept as
# `tickets/done/T0016-red-sportster-candidate.ts`.
#
# `!blueprints/vehicules/red-sportster/generated/qwen3D-01.ts` was the first exception, because the
# scene viewer's manual check opens it. The line 12 of that file was repaired by hand: it held
# `new THREE.Mesh[]`, which does not parse. See tickets/review/T0015-scene-viewer.md.
!blueprints/*/*/generated/*.ts
!blueprints/*/*/generated/.qwen3d-coder-asset.counter

# Secrets and dependencies
*.env.local
node_modules/

# Drafts are local research; only promoted subjects are committed.
blueprints/drafts/

# Editor and OS junk.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Scratch files of an agent session. Throwaway by definition: never committed, and never the only
# copy of something a human must see. See AGENTS.md, "File rules".
.tmp/

# Generated reports: the overlays, the scratches and the contact sheets a check writes for a human.
# Local evidence, rebuilt at any time; never committed.
test-reports/

# Blender backup files.
*.blend1

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
